# 1. Variables

A variable is a named location used to store data.

### Syntax

```python
variable_name = value
```

### Example

```python
name = "Diksha"
age = 22
cgpa = 8.75
is_student = True

print(name)
print(age)
print(cgpa)
print(is_student)
```

### Output

```
Diksha
22
8.75
True
```

---

# 2. Variable Naming Rules

### Valid

```python
student_name = "Rahul"
total_sales = 50000
city = "Pune"
```

### Invalid

```python
2name = "Rahul"

student name = "Rahul"

class = "MBA"
```

